From ddd7df38920497bb380cb621b094956fce101ac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:37:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 181/269] gallium/pvr: verify the geometry stream against a
 captured reference

Captured the geometry static stream from the working Vulkan driver (PVR_CSB_DUMP, open driver bound):

  00000028 00000000 003bf000 00000080 0001c400 00000020 00000202 00020000 20010000 00000000

40 bytes, 10 dwords - the size the builder already produced. The probe now compares every dword that is
fully determined by its inputs, and it matched on the first corrected run: the stream header (dw0/1),
CR_VDM_CTRL_STREAM_BASE (dw2/3, address 0x80003bf000 stored directly), CR_TPU_BORDER_COLOUR_TABLE_VDM
(dw4/5, address 0x8000071000 stored compacted >>2), CR_PPP_CTRL (dw6 = 0x202, wclampen + fixed_point)
and KMD_STREAM_VIEW_IDX (dw9 = 0). dw7 (CR_TE_PSG) and dw8 (VDMCTRL_PDS_STATE0) encode runtime values
the capture does not preserve, so they are printed rather than asserted.

Two things the capture settled that source reading alone had wrong or ambiguous:

 - CR_TPU_BORDER_COLOUR_TABLE_VDM is bits [0:37] and its generated packer compacts the byte address by
   2, while CR_VDM_CTRL_STREAM_BASE is bits [2:39] and stores it directly. My first comparison "failed"
   purely because I fed the compacted value (0x200001c400) as the input; the builder was already right,
   and the real address was 0x8000071000. An external reference catches exactly this class of mistake.
 - the stream really is 40 bytes with a 2-dword KMD_STREAM_HDR, not the 1-dword header the other
   streams use.

The capture also confirms the gating lesson: pvrsrvkm's refcount took 36 seconds to reach 0 before the
switch. The hand-rolled script that crashed the board earlier never waited for it.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
index 1057ecab..28103921 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr_native/pvr_probe.c
@@ -2198,6 +2198,41 @@ csb_check(int fd, struct pipe_screen *pscreen)
                 ggot, gwant_dw);
       }
 
+      /* The geometry stream against the capture taken from the working driver:
+       *   00000028 00000000 003bf000 00000080 0001c400 00000020 00000202 00020000 20010000 00000000
+       * The header, both address packets, CR_PPP_CTRL and the view index are fully determined by the
+       * inputs, so they are compared byte for byte - an external reference, not a self-check. dw7
+       * (CR_TE_PSG) and dw8 (VDMCTRL_PDS_STATE0) encode runtime values (region_stride, forcenewstate,
+       * usc_common_size) that the capture does not preserve, so they are printed, not asserted. */
+      {
+         static const uint32_t cg[10] = {
+            0x00000028u, 0x00000000u, 0x003bf000u, 0x00000080u, 0x0001c400u,
+            0x00000020u, 0x00000202u, 0x00020000u, 0x20010000u, 0x00000000u,
+         };
+         uint8_t gs[256];
+         const uint32_t g = pvr_geom_static_stream(gs, sizeof(gs), 0x80003bf000ull, 0x8000071000ull,
+                                                   false, 0, false, 0, 0);
+         const uint32_t *gd = (const uint32_t *)gs;
+         static const unsigned det[] = { 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9 };
+         bool ok = (g == 40);
+
+         for (unsigned i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(det); i++)
+            if (gd[det[i]] != cg[det[i]])
+               ok = false;
+         if (!ok) {
+            printf("csb:           FAIL: geometry stream differs from the capture where it is determined "
+                   "by its inputs\n");
+            for (unsigned i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(det); i++)
+               printf("csb:             dw%u got %08x capture %08x%s\n", det[i], gd[det[i]],
+                      cg[det[i]], gd[det[i]] == cg[det[i]] ? "" : "   <-- differs");
+            goto out;
+         }
+         printf("csb:           geometry stream MATCHES the capture at the header, both address packets, "
+                "CR_PPP_CTRL and the view index; dw7 TE_PSG %08x (capture %08x), dw8 PDS_STATE0 %08x "
+                "(capture %08x) - runtime inputs, reported not asserted\n",
+                gd[7], cg[7], gd[8], cg[8]);
+      }
+
       printf("csb:           region headers: 64x64 -> 1, 256x64 -> 2, 2x2 macrotiles -> 4, "
                 "800x600 -> %u units, zero tile size refused\n", d);
       }
